    "title": "4/20 food deal alert: KFC, Chipotle, Blaze Pizza, Wingstop, Subway",
    "text": "Jimmy John's is leaning into the 420 theme with a buy-one-get-one-free offer on its Dream Rotation Meal. RiverNorthPhotography/Getty ImagesIf you’re looking to score a cheap bite on 4/20, a handful of national chains are rolling out limited-time deals, from $4.20 sweets and pot pies to buy-one-get-one meals and shareable bundles. Blaze Pizza: The pizza joint is offering the BFF Bundle for $25.99 (online only via app or website, participating locations). The meal deal includes two build-your-own 11-inch pizzas, two fountain drinks and two desserts.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢Chipotle: The deal isn’t officially tied to 4/20, but it works: customers who show up in a hockey jersey after 3 p.m. can score a buy-one-get-one entrée, an easy win for anyone looking to satisfy a serious craving.Insomnia Cookies: A six-pack of classic cookies is priced at $4.20 for the occasion.KFC: The eatery is offering a $4.20 Pot Pie Combo that includes a medium drink. You can also nab two pieces of Original Recipe or Extra Crispy chicken or two tenders for $2.95. The new $20 Chick N’ Nug Meal debuts today, which includes six pieces bone-in chicken, 12 nuggets, two large sides and four biscuits.Make the Times Union a Preferred Source on Google to see more of our journalism when you search.Add Preferred SourceJimmy John’s: The brand is leaning into the theme with a buy-one-get-one-free offer on its Dream Rotation menu, the choices of which mainly include a sandwich, chips and a Cereal n' Milk Crispy Treat. Use code DREAMROTATION to score the deal — valid on up to five meals — making it an easy option for sharing.Article continues below this adBy signing up, you agree to our Terms Of Use and acknowledge that your information will be used as described in our Privacy Policy.Red Robin: Today only, for only $20, guests can snag the Sky-High Towering Trio featuring one Towering Double Cheeseburger Slider Tower, one Towering Onion Ring Shorty and one Cinnamon Sugar Doh. Wingstop: The Hot Box, returning just for 4/20, features a choice of three tenders or eight wings with Fiery Nacho seasoning, along with fries and a 20-ounce drink. Bonus: 420 limited-edition collectible trays available at select locations, while supplies last.Subway: Another not necessarily tied to the day, Subway is offering BOGO free footlong subs through April 28 when you order through the Subway app or website with FLBOGO.April 20, 2026|Updated April 20, 2026 2:18 p.m.Shannon Fromma is a lifelong Capital Region resident currently residing in Wilton with her husband and two rapidly growing children. She received her degree in communications and journalism from the University at Albany in 1999. Before she had a chance to mount her diploma, she accepted a part-time gig writing obituaries for the Times Union. Her role has transformed over the years. Fromma currently pens Shopportunist, a frugal-living column and award-winning blog. Contact her at sfromma@timesunion.com or 518-454-5340.",
